## Metadata
- Author: [[Tanner Higgin]]
- Full Title: It’s Time to Ditch the Idea of Edtech Disruption. But What Comes Next?
- Category: #articles
- Summary:: Edtech's promise of disruption in education has fallen short due to lack of evidence, widening equity gaps, and burnout among teachers and students. The focus on technocentrism in edtech needs to shift towards an ecological perspective that values context, human interaction, and classroom culture. To improve edtech effectiveness, research methods should align with this ecological view, and schools must prioritize technologies that support classroom goals and positive cultures.
